.TH MESH:UPDATE 1 "2026-07-11" "SPP WebOS" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
mesh:update \- Updates features for an existing mesh route.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php mesh:update
.IR uri
[\-\-add-feature=X] [\-\-remove-feature=Y]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mesh:update
command allows you to seamlessly modify the "A La Carte" features injected into a legacy application mounted via the SPP Mesh Router. Instead of forcing you to unmount and remount an application just to toggle a feature, this command safely applies the delta updates to the YAML registry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.IR uri
The URL route that is currently mounted in the Mesh (e.g. /blog).
.TP
.B \-\-add-feature=
The name of a feature to inject (e.g. hardware_quota). Can be used multiple times.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-feature=
The name of a feature to remove (e.g. ui_mesh). Can be used multiple times.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
1. Parses the etc/mesh.yml file into a structural array.
.br
2. Locates the specified route definition and safely modifies the features array.
.br
3. Overwrites the YAML file and automatically triggers a KernelCompiler::compile() to ensure the routing cache is instantly refreshed for subsequent web requests.
